	<text xml:lang="en">
		<body>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><head coords="1,78.00,212.88,96.99,12.00">I. Introduction</head><p coords="1,78.00,237.52,434.32,10.50;1,91.66,252.52,409.76,10.50;1,92.38,267.52,4.79,10.50;1,111.54,267.52,4.79,10.50"><s coords="1,78.00,237.52,434.32,10.50;1,78.00,252.52,18.21,10.50">Self-attention based models have become the standard for sequence transduction <ref type="bibr" coords="1,78.00,252.52,13.66,10.50" target="#b0">[1]</ref>.</s><s coords="1,99.55,252.52,401.87,10.50;1,78.00,267.52,38.33,10.50">Pre-trained encoders and deep residual networks have been widely adopted <ref type="bibr" coords="1,78.00,267.52,14.38,10.50" target="#b1">[2]</ref>- <ref type="bibr" coords="1,97.17,267.52,14.38,10.50" target="#b3">[4]</ref>.</s></p></div>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><head coords="1,78.00,290.88,68.86,12.00">II. Method</head><p coords="1,78.00,315.52,283.96,10.50;1,378.96,315.52,119.37,10.50;1,78.00,330.52,192.50,10.50;1,287.50,330.52,4.55,10.50"><s coords="1,78.00,315.52,305.51,10.50">A pre-trained encoder is fine-tuned on the target data <ref type="bibr" coords="1,365.30,315.52,13.66,10.50" target="#b1">[2]</ref>.</s><s coords="1,386.85,315.52,111.48,10.50;1,78.00,330.52,214.05,10.50">Residual connections stabilise the training of deep models <ref type="bibr" coords="1,273.84,330.52,13.66,10.50" target="#b2">[3]</ref>.</s></p></div>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><head coords="2,78.00,80.88,72.19,12.00">III. Results</head><p coords="2,78.00,105.52,345.42,10.50;2,440.42,105.52,36.78,10.50;2,78.00,120.52,220.43,10.50"><s coords="2,78.00,105.52,366.97,10.50">Recurrent networks remain a strong baseline for short sequences <ref type="bibr" coords="2,426.76,105.52,13.66,10.50" target="#b3">[4]</ref>.</s><s coords="2,448.31,105.52,35.32,10.50;2,78.00,120.52,220.43,10.50">Table <ref type="table" coords="2,480.54,105.52,3.10,10.50" target="#tab_0">I</ref> summarises the accuracy of both models.</s></p></div><figure xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" type="table" xml:id="tab_0" coords="2,78.00,143.16,279.73,68.00"><head>TABLE I .</head><label>I</label><figDesc><div><p><s coords="2,117.77,143.16,239.97,9.00">Accuracy of the baseline and the fine-tuned encoder.</s></p></div></figDesc><table coords="2,84.00,166.16,141.11,45.00"><row><cell>Model</cell><cell>Accuracy</cell></row><row><cell>Baseline LSTM</cell><cell>81.2</cell></row><row><cell cols="2">Fine-tuned encoder 88.7</cell></row></table></figure>
		</body>
